1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,360
Quentin Tarantino, one of the most acclaimed filmmakers of all time, known for bringing

2
00:00:04,360 --> 00:00:09,040
his bold ideas to life with surreal visuals and mind-bending storytelling.

3
00:00:09,040 --> 00:00:11,160
But he wasn't always a Hollywood icon.

4
00:00:11,160 --> 00:00:14,520
Once he was just an ordinary guy working at a video store.

5
00:00:14,520 --> 00:00:17,000
Until one night he decided to rewrite his story.

6
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:22,200
And there was like one night, stay up all night long and rather than give myself excuses,

7
00:00:22,200 --> 00:00:27,100
I would look at everything that I'm up in my life or everything I'm not doing or whatever

8
00:00:27,100 --> 00:00:29,940
and just not give myself any excuses out.

9
00:00:29,940 --> 00:00:30,940
Just like nail it.

10
00:00:30,940 --> 00:00:35,939
And I would spend like all night laying out everything I'm doing that's wrong.

11
00:00:35,939 --> 00:00:38,779
And then I would spend the last two hours figuring out how I can change it.

12
00:00:38,779 --> 00:00:43,580
And as opposed to just doing it and then going to get some sleep, I decided to change my

13
00:00:43,580 --> 00:00:44,580
life.

14
00:00:44,580 --> 00:00:46,580
Today I present you the Tarantino method.

15
00:00:46,580 --> 00:00:51,419
To follow this process, you'll need three things, a pen, a notepad and the dead of night.

16
00:00:51,419 --> 00:00:55,500
When the world is silent and now the soul is awake, that's when it can happen.

17
00:00:55,500 --> 00:00:56,500
Trust.

18
00:00:56,500 --> 00:01:00,060
When it begins, the first page is always going to be the hardest, but it's really all about

19
00:01:00,060 --> 00:01:03,180
getting that ball rolling.

20
00:01:03,180 --> 00:01:08,660
Now that you've started, you have to ask yourself the big, scary, fear mongering question.

21
00:01:08,660 --> 00:01:10,620
What am I doing wrong?

22
00:01:10,620 --> 00:01:11,900
Be brutally honest.

23
00:01:11,900 --> 00:01:14,900
As Quentin himself would say, nail it.

24
00:01:14,900 --> 00:01:15,900
Take your time.

25
00:01:15,900 --> 00:01:16,940
Dive deep.

26
00:01:16,940 --> 00:01:17,940
It's gritty.

27
00:01:17,940 --> 00:01:20,900
It's tough, but it's absolutely necessary.

28
00:01:20,900 --> 00:01:27,059
And when you push through, boom, you're halfway there.

29
00:01:27,059 --> 00:01:28,180
It's all out there.

30
00:01:28,180 --> 00:01:33,620
The fears, the doubts, the mistakes, the lessons, the heartbreak, all laid out, bare for you

31
00:01:33,620 --> 00:01:39,540
to see, not built up in your mind, but on paper, tangible.

32
00:01:39,540 --> 00:01:44,660
Take a moment because now you have to ask yourself, how can I change it?

33
00:01:44,660 --> 00:01:46,639
We're not all Quentin Tarantino.

34
00:01:46,639 --> 00:01:48,959
You might be feeling like you're all written out.

35
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:54,519
So let's make this part simple, a straightforward list, a hundred ways you can change your life.

36
00:01:54,519 --> 00:01:56,360
Quite a simple process.

37
00:01:56,360 --> 00:01:59,919
Take a mistake you've learned and write down a way to change it.

38
00:01:59,919 --> 00:02:03,440
Repeat it over and over again and push forward.

39
00:02:03,440 --> 00:02:04,440
Write it down.

40
00:02:04,440 --> 00:02:10,279
Adapt, reflect, learn, and grow until finally, when you ask yourself, how can I change my

41
00:02:10,279 --> 00:02:11,279
life?

42
00:02:11,279 --> 00:02:12,279
You'll have a hundred ways to do it.

43
00:02:12,279 --> 00:02:15,759
But there's one very important thing you need to remember throughout this whole night.

44
00:02:15,759 --> 00:02:17,759
You gotta actually f***ing do it.


